@startuml Feature Flag Evaluation

' ============================================================================
' Feature Flag Evaluation Sequence Diagram
' ============================================================================
' This diagram shows the flow when evaluating a feature flag for a user.
'
' Endpoint: GET /flags/{key}/evaluate/{user_id}
'
' Evaluation priority (highest to lowest):
' 1. User Override: If user has a specific override, use it
' 2. Global Enable: If flag.enabled=true, return enabled
' 3. Rollout: Check stored assignment or create new one (idempotent)
' 4. Disabled: Default state if none of above match
'
' Database storage ensures:
' - Same user always gets same result for same flag
' - Consistent rollout across multiple servers
' - Idempotent: random decision stored on first request
'
' Caching: Results cached for 1 minute to reduce DB load
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor DarkGreen
    ActorBorderColor DarkGreen
    LifeLineBorderColor DarkGreen
    ParticipantBackgroundColor LightGreen
    ParticipantBorderColor DarkGreen
}

title Feature Flag Evaluation Flow (Repository Pattern)

actor Client
participant "Router\n(feature_flags.py)" as Router
participant "Auth" as Auth
participant "Cache" as Cache
participant "FeatureFlagRepository\n(interface)" as Repo
participant "SQLAlchemy\nImplementation" as Impl
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

Client -> Router : GET /flags/{key}/evaluate/{user_id}\n[Authorization: Bearer token]
Router -> Auth : Validate token
Auth --> Router : Token valid

Router -> Cache : Check cache\nkey: "flag_eval:{key}:{user_id}"

alt Cache Hit
    Cache --> Router : Cached result
    Router --> Client : 200 OK

else Cache Miss
    Cache --> Router : Not found

    Router -> Repo : get_by_key(key)
    Repo -> Impl : get_by_key()
    Impl -> DB : SELECT feature_flag
    DB --> Impl : Flag data
    Impl --> Repo : FeatureFlagEntity
    Repo --> Router : FeatureFlagEntity

    alt User Override Check
        Router -> Repo : get_user_override(flag_id, user_id)
        Repo -> Impl : get_user_override()
        Impl -> DB : SELECT override
        DB --> Impl : Override data
        Impl --> Repo : FeatureFlagOverrideEntity | None
        Repo --> Router : Override | None

        alt Override Found
            Router --> Router : enabled = override.enabled\nreason = "user_override"

        else Flag Globally Enabled
            Router --> Router : enabled = true\nreason = "global"

        else Rollout Percentage > 0
            Router -> Repo : get_rollout_assignment(flag_id, user_id)
            Repo -> Impl : get_rollout_assignment()
            Impl -> DB : SELECT rollout_assignment
            DB --> Impl : Assignment | None
            Impl --> Repo : RolloutAssignmentEntity | None
            Repo --> Router : Assignment | None

            alt Assignment Found
                Router --> Router : enabled = assignment.enabled
            else No Assignment (First Request)
                Router --> Router : enabled = random() < rollout_percentage
                Router -> Repo : create_rollout_assignment(flag_id, user_id, enabled)
                Repo -> Impl : create_rollout_assignment()
                Impl -> DB : INSERT rollout_assignment
                DB --> Impl : Created
                Impl --> Repo : RolloutAssignmentEntity
                Repo --> Router : Assignment stored
            end

            alt Enabled
                Router --> Router : reason = "rollout"
            else Disabled
                Router --> Router : reason = "disabled"
            end

        else
            Router --> Router : enabled = false\nreason = "disabled"
        end
    end

    Router -> Cache : Store result (TTL: 1min)
    Cache --> Router : Cached

    Router --> Client : 200 OK\n{"key": "...", "enabled": true/false, "reason": "..."}
end

note right of Repo
  **Repository Pattern:**
  - get_by_key() returns Entity
  - get_user_override() for overrides
  - get_rollout_assignment() for rollout
  - create_rollout_assignment() stores decision
  - No SQLAlchemy in Router
end note

note left of Router
  **Evaluation Priority:**
  1. User Override (DB)
  2. Global Enable (flag.enabled)
  3. Rollout (stored in DB, idempotent)
  4. Disabled (default)

  **Idempotency:**
  Same as experiment assignments -
  random decision stored on first request,
  subsequent requests return stored value.
end note

@enduml
